<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/styles/checkout.css" />
    <title>Buy Now Pay Later (BNPL) Demo</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <header>
        <h1>Buy Now Pay Later (BNPL) Integration</h1>
        <p style="color: #666; margin-top: 10px;">
          Demonstrating PayPal and Pay Later buttons with BNPL messaging
        </p>
      </header>
      
      <!-- Integration Details Section -->
      <div style="background: #f0f8ff; border: 1px solid #b8daff; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #004085;">Integration Pattern</h3>
        <ul style="margin: 10px 0; color: #004085; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Merchant Type:</strong> Bidding Website / Custom E-commerce</li>
          <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> Vite + React SPA (simulated with vanilla JS here)</li>
          <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js/Express with PayPal Server SDK v2</li>
          <li><strong>Integration:</strong> PayPal JS SDK with <code>enable-funding=paylater</code></li>
          <li><strong>Features:</strong> BNPL messaging, PayPal & Pay Later buttons</li>
        </ul>
        <div style="background: #fff3cd; border: 1px solid #ffc107; border-radius: 4px; padding: 12px; margin-top: 15px; color: #856404;">
          <strong>⚠️ Note:</strong> Both buttons provide the same functionality. This is expected behavior - 
          the Pay Later button is a visual prompt for customers who specifically want to see financing options, 
          but both buttons open the same PayPal experience where Pay Later is available if eligible.
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="checkout-layout">
        <!-- Left Side: Order Summary -->
        <div class="checkout-left">
          <div class="order-summary">
            <h3>Order Summary</h3>
            <div class="order-row">
              <span>Item (Bidding Platform Item):</span>
              <span>$<span id="cart-total">250</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="order-row">
              <span>Shipping:</span>
              <span>$<span id="shipping-amount">10.00</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="order-row total">
              <span>Total:</span>
              <span>$<span id="amount-total">260</span></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <!-- PayPal Pay Later Messaging -->
          <div style="margin: 20px 0;">
            <h4 style="margin-bottom: 10px; color: #333;">Financing Available</h4>
            <div
              data-pp-message
              data-pp-style-layout="text"
              data-pp-style-logo-type="inline"
              data-pp-style-text-color="black"
              data-pp-style-text-size="12"
              data-pp-amount="260"
              data-pp-placement="payment">
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <!-- Integration Notes -->
          <div style="background: #e7f3ff; border-left: 4px solid #0070ba; padding: 15px; margin-top: 20px;">
            <h4 style="margin-top: 0; color: #0070ba;">Developer Notes</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9em; margin: 5px 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              <strong>SDK Configuration:</strong><br>
              • Query param: <code>enable-funding=paylater</code><br>
              • Both buttons use the same <code>createOrder</code> callback<br>
              • Pay Later eligibility determined by PayPal based on cart total, buyer location, and account status<br>
              • Messaging component automatically shows financing terms when eligible
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Right Side: Payment Section -->
        <div class="checkout-right">
          <div class="payment-section">
            <h3>Choose Payment Method</h3>
            
            <!-- Payment Buttons -->
            <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; margin-top: 20px;">
              <!-- PayPal Button -->
              <div style="border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; background: white;">
                <label style="display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600; color: #333;">
                  PayPal (includes Pay Later option)
                </label>
                <div id="paypal-button-container"></div>
              </div>
              
              <!-- Pay Later Button -->
              <div style="border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; background: white;">
                <label style="display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 600; color: #333;">
                  Pay Later (same functionality as PayPal)
                </label>
                <div id="paylater-button-container"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <!-- Behavior Explanation -->
            <div style="margin-top: 20px; padding: 15px; background: #f9f9f9; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;">
              <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
                <strong>Expected Behavior:</strong> Both buttons open the same PayPal checkout window. 
                If the buyer is eligible for Pay Later financing, they'll see that option in the payment 
                selection screen. The separate Pay Later button serves as a visual cue to attract customers 
                interested in financing options.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Result Display -->
      <div id="result-message" style="margin-top: 30px; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; display: none;"></div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- PayPal SDK with Pay Later enabled -->
    <script
      src="https://www.paypal.com/sdk/js?client-id=<%= clientId %>&components=buttons,messages&enable-funding=paylater&currency=USD"
      data-sdk-integration-source="developer-studio">
    </script>
    <script src="/bnpl.js" type="module"></script>
  </body>
</html>
